            "last",
            "few",
            "years",
            "infinite-width",
            "theory",
            "given",
            "remarkably",
            "clean",
            "answers"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c2_but_catch_all_describes_network",
          "text": "But there is a catch: all of this describes a network's output. It says nothing about the network's input-output Jacobian, the object that captures how smooth the network is.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "but",
            "catch",
            "all",
            "describes",
            "network",
            "output",
            "says",
            "nothing",
            "about",
            "network"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c3_smoothness_exactly_what_care_about",
          "text": "And smoothness is exactly what we care about when we want robustness to noise or to adversarial attacks.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "smoothness",
            "exactly",
            "what",
            "care",
            "about",
            "when",
            "want",
            "robustness",
            "noise",
